<doxygen xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="compound.xsd" version="1.9.8" xml:lang="en-US">
  <compounddef id="Print-example" kind="example">
    <compoundname>Print</compoundname>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Generate statistics string. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Generate statistics string<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>buffer</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Character buffer to write statistics to </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>buffer_size</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Size of buffer in bytes </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>true if statistics were written successfully, false on error</para>
</simplesect>
Writes human-readable statistics about the HeapAllocator to the provided buffer. Since HeapAllocator doesn&apos;t track allocations, the statistics primarily describe the allocator type and configuration.</para>
<para>Returns false if:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>buffer is nullptr</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>buffer_size is 0</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>buffer is too small for the statistics string</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>statistics <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classcslt_1_1HeapAllocator" kindref="compound">cslt::HeapAllocator</ref><sp/>allocator(64);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">char</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>buffer[512];</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">if</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(allocator.stats(buffer,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">sizeof</highlight><highlight class="normal">(buffer)))<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>printf(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;%s\n&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>buffer);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Output:</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>HeapAllocator<sp/>Statistics:</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/><sp/><sp/>Type:<sp/>DYNAMIC</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/><sp/><sp/>Default<sp/>Alignment:<sp/>64<sp/>bytes</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/><sp/><sp/>Memory<sp/>Model:<sp/>System<sp/>Heap<sp/>(operator<sp/>new/delete)</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/><sp/><sp/>Note:<sp/>HeapAllocator<sp/>is<sp/>a<sp/>wrapper<sp/>around<sp/>system<sp/>allocator.</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>It<sp/>does<sp/>not<sp/>own<sp/>or<sp/>track<sp/>memory;<sp/>all<sp/>allocations</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>are<sp/>managed<sp/>directly<sp/>by<sp/>the<sp/>OS<sp/>heap.</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> <programlisting filename="Print"></programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
